*.out
*.log
logs/
outputs/
__pycache__

# Claude Code local state (per-developer settings, worktrees, symlinks into cooper/).
# `.claude/*` rather than `.claude/` so git still descends and the two tracked
# subdirectories below can be re-included: the agent and skill definitions are shared
# convention, not per-developer state.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/

# save_plot writes a gallery index.php into every directory it saves a plot to.
studies/**/index.php

# Figures inside study/task directories. They ARE published (webpublish_study.sh
# symlinks the working tree, so untracked files are live on the web) but they are
# not committed: a single validation round is ~250 png + 250 pdf, ~30 MB, and it
# repeats. The script that made them and save_plot's per-plot .log are tracked,
# so a lost figure is one rerun away. Already-tracked images stay tracked.
studies/**/*.png
studies/**/*.pdf
studies/**/*.svg

# LaTeX summaries: summary_pdf.py builds in a temp dir, but a bare pdflatex run or a failed
# build (which keeps SUMMARY.log; *.log is ignored above) can leave these behind.
studies/**/*.aux
studies/**/*.toc
studies/**/*.fls
studies/**/*.fdb_latexmk
studies/**/*.synctex.gz

# Private third-party inputs (author data files, covariances, unpublished notebooks) never go into
# git or a study directory: they live on the group data area (<dirname(getDataPath())>/..., e.g.
# /scratch/submit/cms/wmass/lattice/ASWZ2024/) and are referenced by path. These rules are a
# backstop for copies that already exist in working trees.
studies/lattice-cs-kernel/260923-lattice-data-refit/data/
studies/**/data/CS_*.csv
studies/**/CS_lattice_results/
